 | **Lessons** | 56 lessons with quizzes. 3.11.0 added ten in `js/data/lessons-2.js`: conditionals, reported speech, maki- / makipag- / mag- -an, accidental ma- and mapa-, plurals, location, relative clauses, spoken short forms, Spanish-derived numbers, exclamations (six quiz items each). Before that 46 grammar (3.10.0 added ten picture lessons in `js/data/lessons-pictures.js`); 36 grammar and culture lessons with quizzes (3.7.0 added demonstratives, connectors, maka-/ma-, magpa-/pa-, requests, hedging and hearsay; 3.8.0 added enclitic order, time words, intensifiers, -an / i- / ipang- focus, noun-making affixes and the kaka- form): markers, focus, aspect, particles, po/opo, numbers/time/money, Taglish, hiya, utang na loob, folk beliefs, idioms of distress, and when your Tagalog is not enough (interviewing alone vs a nurse interpreting, family as informants not interpreters, running an interpreted interview, which rating-scale version goes in the chart). |
 | **Reading** | 17 graded passages (A1–C1) with glossaries and comprehension questions (the B2–C1 ones ask for inference, tone and stance). A Listen first button hides the text so you answer by ear. Print handout per passage: passage, glossary, questions, answer key; English under each paragraph, on its own page, or left out. |
